<title>HONG KONG: Oriental Metals 1996 net down 99 percent.</title>
<headline>Oriental Metals 1996 net down 99 percent.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   0.23	 vs 19.0</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    nil	  vs 3.5</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  36.33 loss vs nil</p>
<p>    Net			    1.28	 vs 100.42</p>
<p>    Turnover		     3,018.42   vs 3,047.25</p>
<p>    Company name		 Oriental Metals (Holdings) Co Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  N/A</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   N/A</p>
<p>NOTE - Metals trading firm Oriental Metals is Authorised by state-owned China National Nonferrous Metals Industry Corp to engage in trading of nonferrous metals.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional gain of HK$11.18 million on partial disposal of long term investment, loss of HK$40.71 million on disposal of an associated company and loss of HK$6.80 million arising from theft.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is nil vs five H.K. cents.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
